      "content": "Even a \"low dose\" of caffeine combined with Ritalin significantly narrows your safety margin for unpredictable side effects, as your body cannot accurately gauge the total stimulant load. Because ADHD medications and caffeine interact to heighten cardiovascular strain, self-experimenting without your doctor's specific clearance puts you at real risk for seizures or severe anxiety during high-stress finals. You should stick to the safety rule of consulting your healthcare provider immediately before adding any stimulant, rather than risking a medical emergency on a guess.",
